    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a decent start but a bit surface-level for a policy round. my students need more meat on the bones. can you expand on the \"national sovereignty\" and \"rule of law\" points specifically? like, what are the philosophical or legal justifications for why strict enforcement is a moral or practical necessity for a functioning state? i want them to have really sophisticated, heavy-hitting arguments they can use to counter the humanitarian-focused rebuttals.",
